Q4. What is a nested if statement? Explain its working with a suitable example.


Answer: A nested if statement means placing one if statement inside another if statement. It is used when a second condition must be checked after the first condition is true.

#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

int main() {
    int age = 20;
    int marks = 70;

    if (age >= 18) {
        if (marks >= 40) {
            cout << "Eligible";
        }
    }

    return 0;
}
